\\  & =4-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=25$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=25} & =4-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =4-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point $(25,80)$ is\n\n$$\nm={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=25}=\\frac{18}{5}.\n$$" 13194139535518 17592186045443 true] [17592186510690 1068 #edb/ref 17592186510688 13194139535518 17592186045443 true] [17592186510690 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139535518 17592186045443 true] [17592186510690 1071 "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=9\\sqrt{x}-2{x}^{3/4}$ at the point $(256,16).$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535518 17592186045443 true] [17592186510690 1072 #uuid "88fecdbc-7bc6-55ea-9ea8-19f24b070e65" 13194139535518 17592186045443 true] [17592186510690 1074 "This time, we'll use $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ notation. First, we compute the derivative, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9\\sqrt{x}-2{x}^{3/4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(9{x}^{1/2}-2{x}^{3/4}) \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}-2\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}{x}^{-1/4} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{x}^{-1/2}-\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{-1/4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $x=256$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=256} & =\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{16}-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point $(256,16)$ is\n\n$$\nm={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=256}=-\\frac{3}{32}.\n$$" 13194139535518 17592186045443 true] [17592186510691 1068 #edb/ref 17592186510697 13194139535518 17592186045443 true] [17592186510691 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139535518 17592186045443 true] [17592186510691 1071 "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=3x-6\\sqrt{x}$ 